## 14. Limitations

The study is based on nine sediment sampling locations distributed along an approximately 28.5 km section of the Escravos River. Consequently, the GIS analysis describes spatial variation among the sampled locations and should not automatically be generalised to the entire Escravos River or Niger Delta.

The elemental measurements are concentrations reported in **mg/kg**. They are not direct measurements of radioactive activity in Bq/kg. Therefore, locations with relatively higher concentrations should be interpreted as locations of geochemical interest rather than automatically classified as areas of radiological contamination or health risk.

The original research also notes that determining whether elemental sources are geogenic or anthropogenic is difficult without detailed local background data. Consequently, the GIS analysis will focus primarily on spatial patterns rather than making unsupported causal conclusions.

## 15. Reproducibility

The GitHub repository is intended to make the GIS workflow transparent and reproducible. The cleaned dataset, project brief, QGIS project and map outputs will be stored together so that the sampling locations and elemental concentration data can be reviewed and reused for subsequent spatial analysis.
